@startuml lifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor transparent

title Stateless System Lifecycle

state "Active" as active
state "Freezing" as freezing
state "Hibernated" as hibernated
state "Restoring" as restoring

[*] --> active : create(blob)

active --> freezing : hibernate()
freezing --> hibernated :\nsnapshot()\nseal()\nstore()
freezing --> active : cancel

hibernated --> restoring : restore()
restoring --> active :\nmaterialize()\nrender()

active --> [*] : destroy()

hibernated --> [*] : gc(eviction\npolicy)

note right of active
  **Running state.**
  Service invocations
  transform the blob.
end note

note right of hibernated
  **Evicted state.**
  Only the blob exists.
  Zero CPU, minimal memory.
end note

note bottom of restoring
  **Progressive restoration:**
  1. Shell (static capture)
  2. Structure (DOM, layout)
  3. Interactivity (JS handlers)
  4. Full state (network, live data)
end note

@enduml
